 and  it felt like we went too far in the  other direction where i didn't feel like  you know tense enough or didn't feel  like you know had enough caution and  the solution actually ended up being  changing the main instrument from piano  to um to a different instrument because  the sound of piano that made this moment  feel a bit too  sensitive or too yeah uh uh emotional  and so i feel like that was a moment i  feel really thankful to have had so  early in my career because that  immediately made me feel like oh  this instrument feels a certain way  especially for this director and so now  i know that like if somebody says  something's too sad it might not be the  piece of music it might just be this  game you know yeah that's that's a good  note can you explain how how you might  compose a new piece of work  yeah i think um  well do you usually sit down to piano or  i know i mean you're a pianist but  sometimes you pick up the guitar or no i  definitely don't pick up any other  instruments i wish i wish i could play  like me playing guitar is a very sad  song  [Laughter]  piano and other various keyboards but  other than that process i was mentioning  earlier about improvising and saying  yeah we're trying to improvise around  feeling oftentimes it's it's um  stepping away from an instrument  completely and just trying to think  about what that feels like and like  honestly kind of like singing to myself  for like thinking about sounds in my own  head where i feel like okay if i felt  this way like what does that sound like  and oftentimes i also started thinking  about what other pieces of music make me  feel that way like  so interesting for me to look at  there are a couple of pieces i  i know that um  directly influenced john williams for  example with like the sound of this  shaksakovic feature like the sound of  this other classical piece and the  emotion that it carried and then how he  was able to  totally do his own thing with that and  so for me i feel